+
+# ipv6-server-name
+
+## Why
+`Flask.run` misparses a bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` by treating the first IPv6 colon as the host-port separator.
+
+## What
+- Parse bracketed IPv6 host:port values so the development server receives an unbracketed IPv6 host and configured port.
+- Retain hostname parsing and explicit port zero behavior.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] `SERVER_NAME="[::1]:8080"` with no explicit `host` or `port` calls the development server with `"::1"` and `8080` — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q`
+- [x] Existing hostname and port-zero cases remain covered by `test_run_from_config` — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q`
