+# ipv6-server-name ledger
+
+### Root cause: implicit-assumption
+
+`Flask.run` assumed the first colon in `SERVER_NAME` separates the host and port. A bracketed IPv6 literal contains colons in its host portion.
+
+Fix: recognize the bracketed IPv6 host boundary before extracting the port. Prevention: regression coverage in `test_run_from_config`.
+
+### Verify: Bracketed IPv6 SERVER_NAME parsing preserves hostname and port-zero behavior
+`pytest -q` exit 127 · tree b372554aee072cd0e7bda17f6877062bed2f28d6
+
+### Verify: Bracketed IPv6 SERVER_NAME parsing passes the Flask basic test suite
+`PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q` exit 0 · tree b372554aee072cd0e7bda17f6877062bed2f28d6
